A||||6||Towmaster5||85 GT
Z||000000||Towmaster5||08-12-99||12:29 AM||||I just bought this car and it had a blown engine. I was wondering about also using a 3.1 to replace the 2.8 but my ouestion is do i need to replace the ecm prom for the bigger engine? Also will a 2.8 block from a rwd 84 lemans work. Thanks Dave
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||08-12-99||02:44 AM||||AFAIK, the old PROM will work with the 3.1 without any problems. However, you should get almost 50hp more out of this engine with the proper PROM... But again AFAIK, nobody makes that PROM so you're stuck with the original.
Z||000002||theogre||08-12-99||07:43 AM||||if the 3.1 is a factory setup, why not grab the prom out of the car the 3.1 was in? Making sure of course that the ECM is the same......... 
Z||000003||Speadraser||08-12-99||06:53 PM||||I think a 2.8 RWD has the starter on the wrong side this might run you into some machining costs.  Hell if you were gonna do that, order a new 3.4 from GM performance and use your heads and intake this also has the starter on the wrong side.
Z||000004||GREENDANO||08-12-99||07:42 PM||||pre '85 2.8 V6's had small main bearings and two piece rear main seals.  This is not a desirable engine for any kind of build-up.  My GT with a 3.2 uses the stock PROM, but I have bumped up the fuel pressure to compensate for the extra displacement.  When swapping PROMs, it is very important to understand the chassis and trans/engine combo that it came out of.  Every car/truck is a little different and usually use a different PROM.  Stock Fiero PROMs work well with increased displacement motors as long as it's not excessive and the cam is not too radical.  If you have a really radical motor (compression, big lift cam, ect...)  A custom PROM would be ideal.  But that takes away the driveability and fun of the V6.<br>  Dan-O
Z||000005||terryk||08-13-99||08:22 AM||||You're not going to get 50HP more out of the 3.1L and a PROM. More like 15HP.<p>The 2.8L prom will work with a 3.1L fine. The BLM will compensate quite a bit. The 3.1L crank requires a different flywheel (neutral balanced). The only pistons available for use with the iron heads is the Camaro 8.5:1, but I've wondered if the U-van 3.1L pistons are 8.9:1. They are iron heads too.<p>Only the 6869 or 7170 ECM proms will work in those ECM's. Period.<p><br>
Z||000006||GREENDANO||08-13-99||10:33 PM||||terryk,<br>Best guess, 40 HP, I have a more aggressive GM performance cam as well as minor performance tricks here and there.  I safely estimate my HP at 190.  It does go very well!!  Never been 1/4 mile tested...Yet...<br>  Dan-O
